Consider this case.
```
create table t(a int, b int, c int, primary key(a,b,c));
insert into t values(1,1,1),(2,2,3);
explain select * from t where (a,b) in ((1,1),(2,2)) and c > 2;
```
We get range: `(1 1 2,1 1 +inf], (2 2 2,2 2 +inf]`

For column `a`, we will get range: `(1, 1], (2, 2]`, but `rowCount, err := col.GetColumnRowCount(sc, []*ranger.Range{&rang}, coll.ModifyCount, col.IsHandle)`  with rang = `(2, 2]` will return 0. And the result of explain will output `estRow 0.0`. So I change it to `[2, 2]`.
